{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature","title":"lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support.md","line":56,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support.tex#lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemannian-metric]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:levi-civita-connection]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemann-curvature-tensor]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:sectional-curvature]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support.tex","label":"lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature","line":75,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Connection and curvature under constant rescaling]\n\\label{lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature}\n\\uses{def:riemannian-metric,thm:levi-civita-connection,\n  def:riemann-curvature-tensor,def:sectional-curvature}\n\n\nFor $c>0$, the metric $g_c=cg$ has pairing\n$\\langle v,w\\rangle_{g_c}=c\\langle v,w\\rangle_g$.  Its Levi-Civita\nconnection and $(1,3)$ curvature tensor agree with those of $g$, while\nits $(0,4)$ curvature form is multiplied by $c$.  If $g$ has constant\nsectional curvature $K$, then $g_c$ has constant sectional curvature\n$K/c$.\n\\end{lemma}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Connection and curvature under constant rescaling] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a636f6e7374616e742d72657363616c696e672d636f6e6e656374696f6e2d637572766174757265\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23thm%3Alevi-civita-connection\">↗ thm:levi-civita-connection</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23def%3Ariemann-curvature-tensor\">↗ def:riemann-curvature-tensor</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23def%3Asectional-curvature\">↗ def:sectional-curvature</a> <p></p>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c&gt;0$\">$c&gt;0$</span>, the metric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_c=cg$\">$g_c=cg$</span> has pairing <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\langle v,w\\rangle _{g_c}=c\\langle v,w\\rangle _g$\">$\\langle v,w\\rangle _{g_c}=c\\langle v,w\\rangle _g$</span>. Its Levi-Civita connection and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(1,3)$\">$(1,3)$</span> curvature tensor agree with those of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span>, while its <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(0,4)$\">$(0,4)$</span> curvature form is multiplied by <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span> has constant sectional curvature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K$\">$K$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_c$\">$g_c$</span> has constant sectional curvature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K/c$\">$K/c$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:constant-curvature-normal-jacobi-profile","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:distance-function-weak-laplacian-reduction","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:levi-civita-connection","title":"thm:levi-civita-connection","label":"thm:levi-civita-connection"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemann-curvature-tensor","title":"def:riemann-curvature-tensor","label":"def:riemann-curvature-tensor"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:sectional-curvature","title":"def:sectional-curvature","label":"def:sectional-curvature"}],"backlinks":[],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature","title":"lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Connection and curvature under constant rescaling]\n\\label{lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature}\n\\uses{def:riemannian-metric,thm:levi-civita-connection,\n  def:riemann-curvature-tensor,def:sectional-curvature}\n\n\nFor $c>0$, the metric $g_c=cg$ has pairing\n$\\langle v,w\\rangle_{g_c}=c\\langle v,w\\rangle_g$.  Its Levi-Civita\nconnection and $(1,3)$ curvature tensor agree with those of $g$, while\nits $(0,4)$ curvature form is multiplied by $c$.  If $g$ has constant\nsectional curvature $K$, then $g_c$ has constant sectional curvature\n$K/c$.\n\\end{lemma}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#